- op: discuss  # 9674
  at: '2026-09-28T14:07:17Z'  # 9674
  by: agent  # 9674
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9674
  clock: 4  # 9674
  nonce: '9674'  # 9674
  message: "DONE in PR #1278 (merged). bash.shell_text() blanks every byte from the start of the line holding the first NUL (so the ZIP header PK\\x03\\x04, which precedes its first NUL on that line, goes too), keeping byte length and newlines. A file with no NUL is returned unchanged. BashAnalyzer.parse_source uses it (the base hook's two rules hold), and so does the cross-source name index. The command-name gate this row proposed is the second line: _plausible_command_name (non-empty, printable, no whitespace) guards the command_launch emission.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE:\n  THE ROW'S REPRO, sbt, shipped io-boundaries at the fix commit vs dev (record ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fisoh_09282026/RESULT.md): 21 chains lost, 0 gained, total_io_edges 342 -> 337. Lost: every malformed command_launch primitive (16, including '' and '\\x06\\x16\\x1e\\x066\\x06VF\\x06Q') plus 2 redirect.<, 2 redirect.> and 1 env.environ. ALL 21 come from the two coursier self-executing JARs. Neither shell prefix contains a redirect, and the lost env read comes from the file whose prefix reads no variable. The launcher prefix's real $JAVA_OPTS read is kept in both arms.\n  On merged dev: a synthetic 'sh prefix + zipfile' launcher reports command_launch ['curl'] (the prefix's real launch). Dev before the fix reported 'curl' plus 'PK\\x03\\x04...' and binary fragments; that was checked as the test's control.\nTests: packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/tests/test_bash_binary_payload.py (9).\n\nALSO FIXED, not in the row: the malformed dst ids ('bash::0-0::external_symbol') went with the names.\nNOT MEASURED: makeself '.run' installers and shar archives take the same path; no corpus instance was looked for."  # 9674
